VERDICT
  The M = 2F-1 column is exactly 2^(F-1) at every F in 4..=10, which is a
  closed form rather than a trend, and no M strictly inside gives zero at
  any of the seven widths.

  The argument behind it is a proof and holds for every F >= 1: the exact
  product of two Q(.F) numerals occupies exactly 2F fraction bits, so any
  M < 2F discards a nonzero low part for some operand pair, and a pair
  whose discarded part lands on a rounding boundary changes the result.
  Nothing in that depends on F.

  WIDENING, stated here and not in 167, per the never-widen-in-place rule:
  167 4.1 widens to `F any` on the argument, with the enumerative half
  staying at `F in {6, 8, 10}` where its own file recorded it, and this
  file extending the enumeration to F in 4..=10.
